---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro'
import BlogPostShell from '../../components/BlogPostShell.astro'
import BlogToolEmbed from '../../components/BlogToolEmbed.astro'

const slug = 'luminous-flux-converter'
const seo = {
  title: 'Luminous flux converter — lumens | maratool',
  description: 'Convert lumens, kilolumens, and candela-steradians instantly. Free browser luminous flux converter.',
  canonical: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
  schema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: 'How to convert lumens, kilolumens, and cd·sr',
    image: 'https://maratool.com/og/converter.svg',
    datePublished: '2026-07-25',
    dateModified: '2026-07-25',
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Marcell Almeida', url: 'https://marcell.com.br' },
    publisher: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'maratool',
      url: 'https://maratool.com',
      logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://maratool.com/favicon.svg' },
    },
    mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    url: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
    description: 'Convert lumens, kilolumens, and candela-steradians instantly. Free browser luminous flux converter.',
  },
  breadcrumbSchema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://maratool.com' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://maratool.com/blog' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'How to convert lumens, kilolumens, and cd·sr', item: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    ],
  },
}
---
<Base {...seo}>
  <Layout>
    <BlogPostShell
      title="How to convert lumens, kilolumens, and cd·sr"
      lead="Type a flux — read lm, klm, mlm, or cd·sr instantly."
      date="July 25, 2026"
      dateIso="2026-07-25"
    >
      <p>Lumens are the headline number on every bulb box. The <a href="/luminous-flux-converter/">Luminous Flux Converter</a> shifts lumen prefixes and shows the underlying candela-steradian identity.</p>

      <BlogToolEmbed slug="luminous-flux-converter" title="Try it — convert luminous flux units" height={440} />

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Pick units</strong> — "Kilolumen (klm)" to "Lumen (lm)", or any other pair.</li>
        <li><strong>Type a value</strong> — the result updates as you type, with swap and copy.</li>
        <li><strong>Copy</strong> — one click, with "Copied!" feedback.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Luminous flux conversion factors</h2>
      <p>Every unit converts through the lumen (the base unit). To convert A → B, multiply by A's factor and divide by B's:</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Unit</th><th>= this many lumens</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr><td>Kilolumen (klm)</td><td>1,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Lumen (lm)</td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Millilumen (mlm)</td><td>0.001</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Candela-steradian (cd·sr)</td><td>1</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>When you need it</h2>
      <p>Sizing rule: living rooms need roughly 10–20 lm per square foot, so a 200 ft² room wants 2,000–4,000 lm total. To turn lumens into brightness on a surface, divide by area — that gives <a href="/illuminance-converter/">lux or foot-candles</a>.</p>

      <h2>Sources & methodology</h2>
      <p>Conversion factors follow <a href="https://www.bipm.org/en/publications/si-brochure" rel="noopener" target="_blank">BIPM SI Brochure</a>; exact-by-definition factors are marked in the tool itself. All math runs client-side in your browser — nothing is uploaded.</p>

      <h2>More conversion guides</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/blog/luminous-intensity-converter/">How to convert mcd to candela and candlepower</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/illuminance-converter/">How to convert lux to foot-candles</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/luminous-energy-converter/">How to convert lumen-seconds, talbots, and lumen-hours</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Or browse everything at once in the <a href="/blog/new-unit-converters/">new unit &amp; sizing converters roundup</a>.</p>

      <hr class="blog-divider" />
      <p class="blog-footer-note">The <a href="/luminous-flux-converter/">Luminous Flux</a> tool is free, runs locally, and never sends your data to a server. More <a href="/converter/">converter tools</a> at <a href="/">maratool.com</a>.</p>
    </BlogPostShell>
  </Layout>
</Base>
